# Cello Suite No. 3 in C major, BWV 1009: Gigue (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a brilliant, rustic gigue in 3/8, one beat to the bar.
# Running eighths and sixteenths, two long bariolage passages over open
# string pedals (a sound like bagpipes), and drone sections with double
# stops. Fast and joyful, the finale of the suite.
#
# Time signature: 3/8 with an eighth-note upbeat, 108 bars (A 1-48,
# B 49-108, each half entered on an upbeat). Mutopia file
# cellosuite3-5.mid, the sixth and last score: checked against
# cellosuite3_6_gigue.ly. The score's two repeats are not in the MIDI,
# so play writes them out.
#
# Range: 90 notes below B2 are lifted an octave. Most are the open G
# pedal (G2) of the bariolage (25-31, 81-91) and the drone (92-100):
# lifted to G3, it sits among the upper notes instead of under them,
# so those passages sound as a high repeated note rather than a low
# drone. The low C of the final chord also goes up an octave.
#
# Tempo: dotted quarter = 76, one beat to the bar; 216 bars with
# repeats, about 2:55. Track times: Mstislav Rostropovich (EMI, 1991)
# 2:51 to 2:59, about 74; his 1955 Prague radio recording 2:39, about
# 81. Confirmed from track listings (assuming both take the repeats,
# which the totals imply).
#
# Structure (score bars, my reading of the Mutopia score):
#   A  1-20   C major, the theme, sequences toward G; D major (20).
#      21-31  Bariolage over open-string pedals (D, then G).
#      32-40  Drone section: double stops over D, G minor colour.
#      41-48  Closing scales, cadence in G major.
#   B  49-56  The theme from G, to A minor (G sharps, 53-56).
#      57-72  D minor and F, then A minor (72).
#      73-80  D, G7 toward C.
#      81-91  Bariolage over the G pedal.
#      92-100 Drone over G, C minor colour (A flat, E flat).
#      101-108 Closing scales, cadence in C major.
#
# Bars as performed (play), numbered along the performance:
#   A 0.67-48.67, A repeat 48.67-96.67 (score x = x+48),
#   B 96.67-156.67 (score x = x+48), B repeat 156.67-216.67
#   (score x = x+108).

pickup 8
tempo 76 4.

play 0.666667-48.666667 0.666667-48.666667 48.666667-108.666667 48.666667-108.666667

dyn 1 f              # A first time
dyn 33 mp            # score 32-40: the minor-coloured drone
dyn 41 f             # score 41-48: the close in G
dyn 48.66 mp         # A repeat, an echo
dyn 81 p             # score 33: the drone, softer still
dyn 89 mp            # score 41: the close
dyn 96.66 f          # B first time
dyn 140 mp           # score 92: the drone over G
dyn 149 f            # score 101: the close in C
dyn 156.66 mp        # B repeat, an echo
dyn 200 p            # score 92: the drone
dyn 209 f            # score 101: full again for the end

rit 3 0.75           # the last three one-beat bars
